# Fixed-width element store rejects an overflowed expression

Verifies `a[0] = a[0] + 1` on an `int8[]` array is rejected instead of storing
the promoted `int16` result. The indexed assignment crosses the array element
representation boundary, so `128` cannot enter an `int8` element.

>>> source
let a: int8[] = [127]
a[0] = a[0] + 1
print(a[0])

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `128` cannot be represented as `int8`

<<< exit
1
